A recorded fixture, and WE are the emitter: this is `apps.integrations.newworld` run on three worked payments, recorded 2026-09-22 by the CR-132-BRC07 New World lane and checked byte-for-byte by tests/test_cr132_newworld_receipts.py. It is evidence of what this code actually produces, not a schema written from their prose — a schema written from prose is a claim.

THE THREE RECEIPTS, AND WHY EACH ONE IS HERE

1 · PMT-2609-0187 — $142.18, ACH, account AC-2026-00036, settling bill INV-2609-00412 in full. ONE distribution: 1200 Accounts receivable, 142.18, DistributionType 2 (Credit). It BALANCES: 142.18 = 142.18. This is the ordinary receipt and it is what this feed carries most of.

2 · PMT-2609-0188 — $200.00 by card, of which $142.18 went against bills and $57.82 was carried as credit. TWO distributions — 1200 Accounts receivable 142.18 and 2400 Customer credit 57.82 — which are our journal entry's two credit legs, unchanged. It BALANCES: 142.18 + 57.82 = 200.00. It is here because it is the case that shows the distributions are the LEGS OF A REAL ENTRY rather than a single number restated.

3 · PMT-2609-0189 — $100.00 across three services, stored as 33.3333 · 33.3333 · 33.3334. Rounded to their two decimals that is 33.33 three times, which is 99.99. **IT IS ONE CENT SHORT AND IT IS SENT ANYWAY, FLAGGED** — PO 2026-09-22, "please send receipt even if it is not balance". Nothing is plugged and no cent is invented; `Receipt.difference` states 0.01 and the response header `X-Receipts-Unbalanced` counts it. It is here because a fixture that only shows the happy case cannot prove the rule the PO actually ruled.

WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES BY WHAT IT DOES NOT CONTAIN

* NO CARD DATA. The four `ReceiptPaymentCreditCardNumber`, `…CreditCardType`, `…CreditCardExpirationDate` and `…CreditCardValidationNumber` attributes are present on every payment node and ALWAYS EMPTY (PO 2026-10-21, option A: "Always write all four as `""`"). Receipt 2 is a CARD payment and it carries ReceiptPaymentType 2 (Charge) and four empty card attributes. Populating any of those four would pull cardholder data into a file and destroy the PCI scoping that keeps card data out of this product entirely. G130 fails the build if one of them carries a value in this directory; until 2026-10-21 it failed if a name appeared at all.
* `DueToDueFromFund` and the distribution-level `ProjectCode1/2/3` are present and EMPTY — ruled empty by the PO on 2026-09-22, never omitted and never zero. An empty optional field is a fact; a plausible value is a lie that reconciles. There are NO project codes on `ReceiptTransactionLevel` since 2026-10-21 (the confirmed template carries them only on the distribution level).
* `ReceiptNumber` is empty on all three. Theirs is 13 characters and ours is 15 (`PMT-2609-0187`), so ours does not fit; they assign one, and our number travels in `ReceiptDescription` where both sides can look it up. A wrong 13-character number would be worse than an absent one because it looks like an answer.

Re-record it ONLY when the projection changes on purpose, in the same commit, and say so here.

